# Line endings are decided here, not by each machine's core.autocrlf.
#
# Without this, a Windows clone checks out CRLF and a macOS or Linux clone
# checks out LF, so the same commit produces different files depending on who
# cloned it. Pinning both sides to LF keeps the working copy identical
# everywhere and stops Git's "LF will be replaced by CRLF" notices.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Rendered assets are binary. Never run line-ending conversion over them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.mp4 binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
